.69l66.34-66.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32L139.31,128Z\"/></symbol><symbol id=\"brand-comb\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"><g fill=\"currentColor\"><rect x=\"80\" y=\"112\" width=\"352\" height=\"112\" rx=\"40\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"64\" height=\"216\" rx=\"32\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"200\" width=\"64\" height=\"216\" rx=\"32\"/><rect x=\"272\" y=\"200\" width=\"64\" height=\"216\" rx=\"32\"/><rect x=\"368\" y=\"200\" width=\"64\" height=\"216\" rx=\"32\"/></g></symbol></svg><header class=\"mast\" id=\"mast\">\n  <div class=\"mast-in\">\n    <a class=\"wordmark\" href=\"/\"><svg class=\"mark\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#brand-comb\"></use></svg>Grooming Dogs</a>\n    <nav class=\"nav\" id=\"nav\" aria-label=\"Main\">\n      <ul class=\"nav-list\" id=\"nav-list\"><li class=\"nav-item\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"nav-btn\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"np-0\">Start here<svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-caret-down\"></use></svg></button><div class=\"nav-panel\" id=\"np-0\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"np-in\"><div class=\"np-intro\"><p class=\"np-h\">Start here</p><p>New to grooming? Learn the full routine, then find out what your dog’s coat needs.</p><p class=\"nav-hint\">Not in the list? Search all 22 guides <kbd>/</kbd></p></div><div class=\"np-links\"><a href=\"/how-to-groom-your-dog-at-home/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-list\"></use></svg><b>The full grooming routine</b><span>The complete at-home grooming routine in the right order: brush, nails, ears, bath and dry, face and teeth, trimming.</span></a><a href=\"/dog-coat-types/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-dog\"></use></svg><b>Dog coat types</b><span>Short and smooth, wiry, double, long and silky or curly?</span></a><a href=\"/how-often-should-you-groom-your-dog/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-calendar-blank\"></use></svg><b>Grooming schedule</b><span>How often to brush, bathe, trim nails, check ears and brush teeth, set by your dog's coat type, with the signs that a task is due and when to book a groomer.</span></a><a href=\"/dog-grooming-glossary/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-book-open\"></use></svg><b>Grooming glossary</b><span>Plain definitions of dog grooming terms (coat types, de-matting, cuts and blades, nails, ears, teeth and groomer jargon), each linked to the full guide.</span></a></div><a class=\"np-feat\" href=\"/dog-coat-types/\"><img src=\"{{IMG:coat-double}}\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><b>Find your dog’s coat type</b><span>Photo: Sergei Starostin / Pexels</span></a></div></div></li><li class=\"nav-item\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"nav-btn\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"np-1\">Grooming tasks<svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-caret-down\"></use></svg></button><div class=\"nav-panel\" id=\"np-1\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"np-in\"><div class=\"np-intro\"><p class=\"np-h\">Grooming tasks</p><p>Step-by-step guides for each job, with the tools and the warning signs.</p><p class=\"nav-hint\">Not in the list? Search all 22 guides <kbd>/</kbd></p></div><div class=\"np-links\"><a href=\"/bathing-your-dog/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-bathtub\"></use></svg><b>Bathing</b><span>Brush your dog first, because water makes mats worse.</span></a><a href=\"/trimming-dog-nails/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-paw-print\"></use></svg><b>Nail trimming</b><span>Hold the toe gently so the nail extends.</span></a><a href=\"/brushing-your-dog/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-sparkle\"></use></svg><b>Brushing</b><span>Brush to the skin, a small section at a time.</span></a><a href=\"/cleaning-dog-ears/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-ear\"></use></svg><b>Ear cleaning</b><span>Clean when you can see dirt or wax build-up.</span></a><a href=\"/dog-haircuts-and-trimming/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-scissors\"></use></svg><b>Haircuts &amp; trimming</b><span>Stick to small, careful trims: hair covering the eyes, long hair around the genitals, and hair between the paw pads.</span></a><a href=\"/brushing-dog-teeth/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-tooth\"></use></svg><b>Teeth brushing</b><span>Start slowly.</span></a></div><a class=\"np-feat\" href=\"/bathing-your-dog/\"><img src=\"{{IMG:lead-bathing}}\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><b>Bathing your dog, step by step</b><span>Photo: David Kanigan / Pexels</span></a></div></div></li><li class=\"nav-item\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"nav-btn\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"np-2\">Your dog<svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-caret-down\"></use></svg></button><div class=\"nav-panel\" id=\"np-2\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"np-in\"><div class=\"np-intro\"><p class=\"np-h\">Your dog</p><p>Puppies, older dogs and nervous dogs need a gentler routine.</p><p class=\"nav-hint\">Not in the list? Search all 22 guides <kbd>/</kbd></p></div><div class=\"np-links\"><a href=\"/puppy-grooming/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-baby\"></use></svg><b>Puppy grooming</b><span>Start early, gently and briefly.</span></a><a href=\"/senior-dog-grooming/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-clock\"></use></svg><b>Senior dogs</b><span>Old age isn't a disease, and your older dog may not need any changes to their grooming.</span></a><a href=\"/grooming-an-anxious-dog/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-heart\"></use></svg><b>Anxious dogs</b><span>Don't force it.</span></a><a href=\"/dog-grooming-problems/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-warning\"></use></svg><b>Problems after grooming</b><span>Stop the grooming task that seems to be causing the problem.</span></a></div><a class=\"np-feat\" href=\"/puppy-grooming/\"><img src=\"{{IMG:lead-puppy}}\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><b>Puppy grooming</b><span>Photo: JacLou- DL / Pexels</span></a></div></div></li><li class=\"nav-item\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"nav-btn\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"np-3\">Tools &amp; groomers<svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-caret-down\"></use></svg></button><div class=\"nav-panel\" id=\"np-3\" hidden=\"\"><div class=\"np-in\"><div class=\"np-intro\"><p class=\"np-h\">Tools &amp; groomers</p><p>What to buy, and how to choose and pay a professional.</p><p class=\"nav-hint\">Not in the list? Search all 22 guides <kbd>/</kbd></p></div><div class=\"np-links\"><a href=\"/dog-grooming-tools/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-towel\"></use></svg><b>Grooming tools</b><span>A brush that suits their coat, plus a comb to check your work;</span></a><a href=\"/choosing-a-dog-groomer/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-shield-check\"></use></svg><b>Choosing a groomer</b><span>Visit before you book.</span></a><a href=\"/dog-grooming-cost/\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-storefront\"></use></svg><b>Grooming cost</b><span>Full groom at a salon: the salons we checked list prices from $55 for a small dog to $200 for an extra-large one, before tax.</span></a></div><a class=\"np-feat\" href=\"/choosing-a-dog-groomer/\"><img src=\"{{IMG:lead-groomer}}\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><b>Choosing a dog groomer</b><span>Photo: Goochie Poochie Grooming / Pexels</span></a></div></div></li></ul>\n    </nav>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"mast-search\" id=\"mast-search\" aria-label=\"Search the guides\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-magnifying-glass\"></use></svg><span class=\"lbl\">Search</span><kbd>/</kbd></button>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"mast-menu\" id=\"mast-menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"nav\"><svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#ph-list\"></use></svg><span class=\"sr-only\">Menu</span></button>\n  </div>\n</header>"
